  "_comment": [
    "GET /3/movie/550?language=en-US&append_to_response=credits,external_ids,",
    "release_dates,watch/providers, trimmed to the fields the mirror reads.",
    "",
    "Confirmed against TMDB's own rendered example responses, fetched",
    "2026-09-16: the top-level movie fields against developer.themoviedb.org",
    "/reference/movie-details, the release_dates block against",
    "/reference/movie-release-dates (including that release_date there is a full",
    "instant rather than a plain date, and that a country repeats an entry per",
    "language), and the provider entry fields against",
    "/reference/movie-watch-providers.",
    "",
    "Inferred rather than confirmed: the JSON key append_to_response nests the",
    "providers under. /docs/append-to-response says only that each sub-request",
    "'appends as a new JSON object' and does not name the keys, and the watch",
    "providers page renders its example as prose. 'watch/providers' verbatim is",
    "what every open-source client reads; the first live run confirms it.",
    "",
    "The US release_dates below deliberately carry two type-3 entries on the",
    "same date differing only in note (a standard run and an IMAX one), which is",
    "a real shape and which media_release_dates' four-column primary key cannot",
    "hold twice. GB is here to be a region with no certification at all.",
    "Provider 1899 (Max) is deliberately absent from tmdb-providers-movie.json,",
    "so the title has to stub it before its own availability row.",
    "",
    "The figures are illustrative; the field names are the part under test."
  ],
